          <span>Moving abroad with a child for good</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/international-child-abduction-uae/" class="service-link">
          <strong>International Child Abduction</strong>
          <span>Prevention and what to do if it happens</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/child-custody-uae/" class="service-link">
          <strong>Child Custody in the UAE</strong>
          <span>Who gets custody and how courts decide</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/visitation-rights-uae/" class="service-link">
          <strong>Visitation Rights</strong>
          <span>Contact schedules and enforcement</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/father-custody-rights-uae/" class="service-link">
          <strong>Father and Mother Rights</strong>
          <span>Custody and guardianship under the 2024 law</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <FAQSection items={faqItems} lang="en" />

    <section class="section section--cta" aria-labelledby="bottom-cta-heading" id="contact">
      <h2 id="bottom-cta-heading">Need a Travel Permit or a Passport Order? Talk It Through</h2>
      <p>Request a free, confidential consultation with a UAE-licensed family lawyer about consent, a court travel permit or a passport handover, in English or Arabic. If a signed letter from the other parent is all you need, that is a perfectly good answer to walk away with.</p>
      <LeadForm lang="en" variant="inline" />
    </section>

  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
